    "notes": "Complete independent equipment-shed interpretation: mapped log walls, low red metal hipped roof, three recessed weathered timber door bays, log corner ends, pale grounded plinth and supported threshold aprons. Plain small plaques retain the placement of the photo panels without copied lettering. Reuse wood_log, wood_vertical, wood_plain, metal_standing_seam, plaster_lime and metal_painted graphs. The neighboring poultry house remains a separate model; no trees, people, copied signs or photo pixels are baked in. Photo-led low log shed: wall2.25m, red hip ridge3.6m above local floor, three genuinely recessed timber door bays, restrained eaves, small plain end plaques and supported threshold aprons. Native ground changes about1.6m across this footprint. The source applies a bounded -.06m/m long-axis visualization grade; this reduces the exposed plinth while retaining one-story proportions, and is not a surveyed historic floor/roof. Exact pitch, door census, panel details and thresholds remain reconstructed. Equipment-shed identity and the southwest three-door face are inferred from the paired museum photograph, relative estate context and larger mapped shed footprint. Both public map names are only sheds. Hidden rear details, door proportions, blank plaques and historic levels remain reconstructed. The retained coarse DEM changes about1.6m across this footprint; a bounded-.06m/m long-axis visualization grade reduces exposed plinth without changing the original terrain. The sloping floor/roof and thresholds are not surveyed historical geometry. The estate service inventory remains unfinished."
